ing to see what with what we're  looking at for the next version of Gears  yeah this wasn't a show we weren't we  just wasn't the right time sure we could  have put together something with no  clear a ship date idea or something I  didn't want to do that  I said let's keep the team focused on  getting the right game idea and then  when we were there and we've got a story  to tell on stage we'll go do that but  this wasn't the right time for it but  I'm incredibly excited about what the  team can do and trying to take gears and  maybe get a little more gritty with the  the IP I think would be a good thing for  it a dream mashup game wow wow that's a  good question I'm gonna have to start  with like probably my most addictive  game that I've ever played in Robotron  so I'm going to start with a dual stick  shooter and then what would I want to  layer on if it had verticality because  it was all 2d and a different character  space I'm gonna go with Robotron  crackdown and I think if you had the  ability to kind of move around with a  dual stick and kind of a top-down view  but jump up on the top of buildings and  destroy buildings and stuff I just made  that up  but maybe we should do dual stick  crackdown meets Robotron
 

